WEBVTT

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
kanashige ni saku hana ni kimi no omokage wo mita

00:00.567 --> 00:09.424
I saw your image in the flower that is blossoming sorrowfully

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
daisuki na ame nanoni naze ka kyou wa tsumetakute

00:09.937 --> 00:18.509
I love rain, yet it felt frosty today

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
kisetsu wa meguri mori wa somerare kaze wa kanadete omoi afurete

00:18.651 --> 00:37.226
The season changed, the forest was colored, the wind played a tune, memories overflowed

00:37.600 --> 00:46.786
tsuki no kakera wo atsumete yume wo kazari nemuru

00:37.600 --> 00:46.787
Gather the pieces of the moon, decorate the dream and sleep

00:47.020 --> 00:56.153
toki no suna chiribametemo ano koro e kaeranai

00:47.020 --> 00:56.154
Even if I sprinkle the sand of time, I cannot return to the past

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
ikiru imi sageshiteiru dare mo mina tabibito

00:56.313 --> 01:05.420
Those searching for the meaning of life are all travellers

01:05.769 --> 01:14.817
haruka naru tabiji tadori boku wa ima arukidasu

01:05.776 --> 01:14.817
I set my course on this endless journey

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
ibara no michi no mukou e...

01:14.837 --> 01:22.812
for the place beyond the thorny path...

01:25.818 --> 01:30.738
The artist of life who produces miracles
with his godlike scalpel skills.

01:31.657 --> 01:33.992
The surgeon whom the era has yearned for.

01:34.868 --> 01:35.911
Black Jack.

02:09.450 --> 02:13.078
I wonder if people will really come
this far into the mountains.

02:13.830 --> 02:16.331
That's not our problem.

02:16.332 --> 02:18.694
We build it. They give us money. That's all.

02:19.001 --> 02:20.752
Give me back this mountain.

02:27.051 --> 02:28.343
That's...

02:46.209 --> 02:47.546
What's this all\about?

02:47.947 --> 02:49.698
What happened on that mountain?

02:50.741 --> 02:53.410
Nadare...

02:55.233 --> 02:58.312
Originally by Tezuka Osamu "Nadare"

02:55.233 --> 02:58.312
A Challenge Named Nadare

03:00.251 --> 03:04.054
Why do neither humans nor animals
become more intelligent?

03:04.463 --> 03:09.340
That is because the brain is stored inside
a hard substance known as the skull.

03:09.760 --> 03:12.888
The skull protects the brain,

03:12.889 --> 03:16.391
but it also limits the brain's growth.

03:17.018 --> 03:19.656
If we put the brain in something other than the skull,

03:20.062 --> 03:22.564
such as the torso, and give it growth hormones,

03:22.565 --> 03:24.351
it will easily expand,

03:24.609 --> 03:27.015
and thus allow an individual to become more intelligent.

03:27.445 --> 03:32.866
The hormone Valmir, which I have created,
stimulates the growth of brain cells.

03:33.910 --> 03:37.204
With this hormone, the brain can
develop new cells rapidly.

03:38.039 --> 03:42.876
Thus, this research will lead to a cure for
children who suffer from brain damage.

03:48.507 --> 03:51.593
That was a wonderful presentation, Dr. Oedo.

03:51.594 --> 03:53.011
I have some good news for you.

03:53.012 --> 03:56.932
Because of your research, you've been nominated
for the Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine.

04:09.445 --> 04:12.030
Doctor, give us a comment about your Nobel Prize.

04:12.907 --> 04:15.018
I haven't been awarded one yet.

04:15.242 --> 04:16.745
What is your research about?

04:16.994 --> 04:20.956
Simply put, the research seeks to
make people more intelligent.

04:21.089 --> 04:23.750
What kind of people does it make more intelligent?

04:23.795 --> 04:25.762
Ones like you.

04:25.909 --> 04:27.659
Oh, that's great!

04:27.660 --> 04:29.411
Has it been tested on humans?

04:29.642 --> 04:32.623
No, it's still being tested on animals.

04:32.624 --> 04:35.125
But if that goes well, you'll eventually test it on humans?

04:35.316 --> 04:39.087
This procedure requires the brain to be extracted
from the head and transplanted into the torso.

04:39.756 --> 04:42.863
It's an extremely difficult surgical operation.

04:43.092 --> 04:45.594
There is only one doctor who can perform it.

04:46.512 --> 04:48.055
And what is that doctor's name?

04:49.349 --> 04:50.515
Daigo,

04:50.516 --> 04:52.309
welcome home,

04:52.310 --> 04:53.935
and congratulations.

04:54.354 --> 04:55.616
Thank you, Mika,

04:56.022 --> 04:57.632
but we'll get congratulated for
something even better soon.

04:58.024 --> 05:00.359
So save it for our wedding.

05:00.578 --> 05:03.320
The good news just keeps coming.

05:05.907 --> 05:09.409
He's been selected as a Nobel Prize
candidate for this research.

05:10.078 --> 05:12.412
What's a Nobel Prize?

05:13.316 --> 05:17.292
It's an award given to people, who discover great things.

05:18.169 --> 05:20.879
How many Nobel Prizes have you gotten, Doc?

05:22.215 --> 05:27.094
Dr. Oedo's research concerns how to stimulate
the growth of the human brain.

05:29.680 --> 05:31.223
Pinoco, look after the house.

05:31.224 --> 05:34.684
It can't be good when you talk like that!

05:34.685 --> 05:35.936
I'm coming too!

05:37.188 --> 05:39.064
It's dangerous, so no.

05:39.065 --> 05:40.023
Dangerous?

05:40.024 --> 05:43.880
Then as your wife, I definitely can't let you go alone!

05:44.028 --> 05:47.239
No matter what kind of danger darling is in,

05:47.240 --> 05:50.742
his wife will save him.

05:50.743 --> 05:53.578
Neither fire nor water...

05:53.579 --> 05:54.413
Hey Largo!

05:54.414 --> 05:56.862
If it's important, use words!

05:59.752 --> 06:02.184
Pinoco, take care of Largo.

06:02.505 --> 06:04.673
Largo, watch after Pinoco.

06:05.716 --> 06:06.842
Hmph.

06:06.843 --> 06:08.969
Jeez, Doc!

06:08.970 --> 06:11.596
How dare you make me lonely!

06:11.597 --> 06:15.350
You better bring me lots of souvenirs!

06:16.227 --> 06:17.144
What?

06:17.145 --> 06:18.770
Do you have something to say?

06:31.117 --> 06:32.697
<i>It's been a year since I've been home.</i>

06:32.910 --> 06:34.661
<i>I wonder how Nadare is doing?</i>

06:36.622 --> 06:38.623
Nadare, I'm home.

06:39.834 --> 06:41.001
Strange...

06:41.002 --> 06:41.986
Nobody's around.

06:48.009 --> 06:50.051
What happened here?

06:51.399 --> 06:52.678
Who did this?

06:53.264 --> 06:55.765
Where's my assistant, Saigo?

07:00.730 --> 07:02.272
Dr. Black Jack!

07:02.273 --> 07:03.273
Why are you here?!

07:03.900 --> 07:06.591
I wanted to talk to you face to face.

07:06.903 --> 07:08.737
Pardon my rudeness, but would you come with me?

07:08.765 --> 07:11.545
Yamaoku Hospital

07:12.116 --> 07:13.491
Saigo-kun!

07:13.492 --> 07:15.076
What happened?!

07:15.328 --> 07:16.883
What happened while I was gone?

07:17.079 --> 07:18.288
Who did this?!

07:19.457 --> 07:21.291
Nadare did...

07:21.709 --> 07:22.794
Nadare?

07:23.252 --> 07:25.128
You mean, Nadare did this?!

07:25.129 --> 07:25.891
Correct.

07:26.172 --> 07:28.757
The same Nadare you loved.

07:29.216 --> 07:31.504
No way!

07:32.178 --> 07:37.359
I warned you back then that anything could happen.

07:39.810 --> 07:40.894
Nadare did...

07:42.521 --> 07:44.975
Both my father and mother were biologists.

07:45.441 --> 07:47.511
After they died, I took over both
their research and their facility.

07:47.777 --> 07:49.778
So I was rather young when I started researching.

07:52.782 --> 07:53.520
Nadare!

07:54.241 --> 07:58.078
My specimen, Nadare, was the only family I had left.

07:58.079 --> 07:58.954
Good boy.

08:00.663 --> 08:04.000
I took care of Nadare as if he were my little brother.

08:08.881 --> 08:10.264
Got one!

08:10.508 --> 08:11.841
See, Nadare?

08:18.307 --> 08:20.975
I wish you could talk like people can.

08:21.519 --> 08:23.866
Then we could be even closer.

08:25.523 --> 08:29.109
So I researched how to develop Nadare's brain further.

08:31.654 --> 08:34.948
Nadare's the only family I have left.

08:35.658 --> 08:37.409
A deer is your only family member?

08:38.285 --> 08:41.496
If only Nadare were as intelligent as a person...

08:43.124 --> 08:47.127
We will extract Nadare's brain from his
skull and transplant it into his chest.

08:47.837 --> 08:50.683
It's still within the same body, so it should work.

08:51.340 --> 08:54.042
What good will that do?

08:54.385 --> 08:58.721
If I give him Valmir, his brain will
quickly develop and grow larger.

08:59.932 --> 09:01.850
He will be just as intelligent as a person.

09:05.729 --> 09:08.314
Sure, the size of his brain may grow.

09:08.315 --> 09:11.860
But I wonder if he will really
become as intelligent as a person.

09:12.139 --> 09:14.410
Theoretically, it should work.

09:14.864 --> 09:18.825
This can be a historic event for
both people and for animals.

09:19.493 --> 09:23.138
Sorry, but I'm not interested in being a part of history.

09:23.497 --> 09:29.252
If this experiment is successful, we might find
a way to cure kids who's brains are damaged!

09:29.712 --> 09:30.795
Please!

09:31.046 --> 09:32.725
I will pay you any amount—no matter how much.

09:33.132 --> 09:37.135
I have twee years worth of funding plus all
of the assets I inherited from my father.

09:38.721 --> 09:40.555
I have a bad feeling about this.

09:41.682 --> 09:45.143
No matter what happens, do not hold me responsible.

10:11.003 --> 10:12.861
The operation should have been successful.

10:13.422 --> 10:15.465
But nothing about Nadare seems different.

10:16.110 --> 10:17.884
The experiment was a failure.

10:19.637 --> 10:21.763
I'll be a laughingstock!

10:22.723 --> 10:25.850
Da... i... go...

10:25.851 --> 10:27.143
Shut up!

10:30.272 --> 10:32.232
Daigo...

10:33.651 --> 10:34.525
Nadare!

10:35.152 --> 10:37.195
You can talk?

10:38.072 --> 10:39.155
Daigo...

10:40.282 --> 10:41.238
Nadare!

10:41.533 --> 10:42.917
My dear brother!

10:49.827 --> 10:50.460
Look at this.

10:50.920 --> 10:52.210
This is the result.

10:57.007 --> 10:57.931
No way!

10:58.217 --> 10:59.759
Nadare didn't do this.

11:00.594 --> 11:02.296
Nadare wouldn't do this!

11:03.097 --> 11:05.455
Then go see it for yourself.

11:07.851 --> 11:10.151
This whole thing was done by one buck.

11:10.646 --> 11:12.304
You can tell by looking at the tracks.

11:14.692 --> 11:17.860
This is... Nadare's hoof print.

11:19.029 --> 11:21.030
Why did he do this?

11:21.031 --> 11:23.074
He was always so friendly around people.

11:23.575 --> 11:27.927
Just as you predicted, Nadare's brain grew.

11:28.122 --> 11:32.390
But as his intelligence grew, so did
his feelings of doubt and hatred.

11:33.001 --> 11:37.839
The humans he thought were his friends were treating
the lab animals harshly and destroying the mountain,

11:37.840 --> 11:40.800
so he changed his mind based on what he saw.

11:42.183 --> 11:45.041
He must shave recognized us as the enemy instinctively.

11:45.431 --> 11:47.974
But the Nadare I know hasn't changed.

11:47.975 --> 11:49.151
He's my brother.

11:49.560 --> 11:52.478
I will solve his misconceptions and
bring back the old Nadare.

11:55.065 --> 11:56.407
This is a deer whistle.

11:56.900 --> 12:00.570
Nadare should come back to me if he hears it.

12:24.595 --> 12:25.915
It doesn't look like he's coming.

12:26.505 --> 12:28.618
He must be waiting for it to get dark.

12:28.891 --> 12:31.058
He's planning to come in the night.

12:31.810 --> 12:35.062
We can't use surgery to turn him
back even if he does come.

12:38.567 --> 12:39.650
The back door!

13:05.986 --> 13:06.965
Nadare!

13:07.779 --> 13:08.904
Daigo.

13:09.781 --> 13:11.495
I'm sorry I was away for so long.

13:11.783 --> 13:13.982
Why didn't you wait here quietly?

13:14.453 --> 13:15.950
You must have been worried, right?

13:16.371 --> 13:18.456
I won't leave you anymore.

13:24.212 --> 13:25.463
Do you not remember who he is?

13:25.672 --> 13:28.632
This is Dr. Black Jack, the man who operated on you.

13:29.676 --> 13:30.943
Black...

13:32.554 --> 13:34.680
I made some dinner for you.

13:36.350 --> 13:37.183
Eat up.

13:39.061 --> 13:40.973
Your appearance has changed quite a bit.

13:41.313 --> 13:43.981
Are you going to return to the wild?

13:44.733 --> 13:45.943
Now, listen.

13:46.193 --> 13:47.629
Don't attack people anymore.

13:47.903 --> 13:49.779
People are living creatures, just like you.

13:50.572 --> 13:53.407
People destroy nature.

13:53.408 --> 13:54.492
That's bad.

13:55.535 --> 13:58.285
Yes, I know there are bad people too.

13:58.622 --> 14:02.458
But people should be the ones to
pass judgement on other people.

14:02.959 --> 14:05.294
People... pass judgment...

14:06.671 --> 14:08.756
Daigo... kind.

14:09.424 --> 14:10.633
Thank you.

14:11.802 --> 14:13.171
Let's live together again.

14:13.470 --> 14:16.430
I'm sure my wife will treat you well too.

14:17.724 --> 14:18.891
Wife...

14:19.286 --> 14:21.311
I'm getting married next month.

14:21.770 --> 14:24.855
We met when we were lab technicians at the university.

14:25.649 --> 14:28.651
She'll be working here as my assistant.

14:30.904 --> 14:32.223
Congratulations.

14:32.447 --> 14:34.198
You finally have another family member.

14:35.242 --> 14:38.661
She's planning to arrive here tomorrow morning.

14:39.454 --> 14:41.413
Wife...

14:47.254 --> 14:48.462
is this OK?

14:48.672 --> 14:50.912
I'll be informing the townsfolk tomorrow.

14:51.258 --> 14:52.255
I know.

14:52.676 --> 14:54.746
But I just want to spend one night with Nadare.

14:55.011 --> 14:57.471
I prepared a room for you upstairs doctor.

15:40.390 --> 15:43.601
Ma'am, this is awfully early to be travelling.

15:44.144 --> 15:46.481
There's a man I'm very eager to see.

15:46.813 --> 15:48.564
I want to get there early and surprise him.

15:55.864 --> 15:56.989
What's that?

16:15.425 --> 16:16.133
Yes.

16:17.474 --> 16:18.385
What?!

16:19.095 --> 16:20.346
This is terrible.

16:24.893 --> 16:26.393
Nadare did this.

16:29.272 --> 16:30.126
Mika!

16:32.359 --> 16:35.819
Nadare must have thought that Mika
would take you away from him.

16:35.820 --> 16:37.650
His jealousy must have turned into rage.

16:38.573 --> 16:39.823
No way!

16:41.117 --> 16:42.307
Do you understand now?

16:42.702 --> 16:45.555
Nadare is no longer the same Nadare you once knew.

16:47.415 --> 16:50.542
The ambulance is having trouble
getting here because of the snow.

16:51.920 --> 16:54.129
She can be saved, but she is in critical condition.

16:54.130 --> 16:55.089
There isn't much time.

16:55.882 --> 16:58.425
Your lab would be the closest place from here, I think.

16:58.707 --> 16:59.760
Let's operate on her there.

17:00.512 --> 17:01.373
Doctor.

17:03.515 --> 17:05.224
Carry the patient gently.

17:06.309 --> 17:09.269
Doctor, we'll start the hunt today.

17:09.270 --> 17:11.124
We will get that monster.

17:11.523 --> 17:13.044
Doctor, please...

17:13.400 --> 17:14.983
Please take care of Mika.

17:25.662 --> 17:26.640
Nadare...

17:26.871 --> 17:28.455
I will get you.

17:36.214 --> 17:38.632
Nadare!

17:50.520 --> 17:53.105
<i>One of her ribs snapped and punctured one of her lungs.</i>

17:53.106 --> 17:54.064
<i>This is going to be difficult.</i>

18:00.530 --> 18:02.441
<i>It's unexpectedly complicated.</i>

18:17.630 --> 18:20.007
You're attacking the wrong people.

18:31.853 --> 18:34.646
<i>Damn it. The patient won't survive for long like this.</i>

18:51.915 --> 18:53.165
Stop it!

19:22.320 --> 19:23.589
Nadare!

19:28.076 --> 19:30.410
Nadare, forgive me.

19:30.411 --> 19:31.995
This is my judgement.

19:34.248 --> 19:36.541
You said last night...

19:37.686 --> 19:40.063
that people should pass judgment on other people.

19:40.088 --> 19:43.048
Then do people have the right
to pass judgement on"animals?

19:58.398 --> 20:00.774
Da... igo...

20:20.711 --> 20:21.586
Nadare!

20:21.587 --> 20:22.782
Don't go after him!

20:23.005 --> 20:25.006
He has his own world.

20:25.800 --> 20:27.797
Don't force him to live in human society.

20:58.875 --> 21:01.512
<i>Nadare has disappeared since that day.</i>

21:02.920 --> 21:05.255
<i>He never attacked another person again.</i>

21:06.215 --> 21:08.258
<i>Did he die?</i>

21:28.696 --> 21:32.824
Sheesh. Largo, you're the ultimate example of laziness.

21:32.825 --> 21:37.704
Hey, Doc, can't you operate on Largo so she'll be smarter?

21:39.373 --> 21:41.777
It's best to leave her as she is.

21:42.126 --> 21:44.711
There's no need trying to make her more like a human.

21:46.797 --> 21:47.797
Hmph!

22:07.079 --> 22:19.034
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

22:07.079 --> 22:19.034
daisukuyo anata to hitotsu ni nareru no nara

22:19.152 --> 22:24.151
I couldn't be happier...

22:19.152 --> 22:24.151
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

22:25.720 --> 22:31.189
I wanted to see you forever

22:25.720 --> 22:31.189
zutto aitakute mattetano

22:31.733 --> 22:37.191
I'm laying on the grill,

22:31.733 --> 22:37.191
ami no ue ni yasashiku nekasete

22:37.795 --> 22:40.280
being heated up by you,

22:37.795 --> 22:40.280
anata ni hoterasarete

22:40.489 --> 22:48.266
so much that I change color

22:40.489 --> 22:48.266
atashi wa iro ga kawarukurai

22:48.351 --> 23:00.120
I dress up with sparkly grains of decorations

22:48.351 --> 23:00.120
kirakira hikaru tsubu no kazari de oshare

23:00.328 --> 23:12.059
I love you darling. Please love me more and more...

23:00.328 --> 23:12.059
daisukiyo motto motto atashi wo aishite

23:12.299 --> 23:23.650
I love you darling. If I can be united with you,

23:12.299 --> 23:23.650
daisukiyo anata to hitotsu no nareru no nara

23:23.836 --> 23:28.757
I couldn't be happier

23:23.836 --> 23:28.757
konna shiawase wa naiwa...

23:28.985 --> 23:33.919
How does it taste?

23:28.985 --> 23:33.918
oaji wa ikaga?

23:45.049 --> 24:15.040
The Cholera Epidemic

23:45.703 --> 23:49.124
Numerous cases of cholera have been reported
among a group of doctors who were traveling.

23:49.323 --> 23:50.770
Where's the medical inspection?

23:52.738 --> 23:55.185
Those who came in contact with this group
of doctors are being infected.

23:55.424 --> 23:56.424
I could have been infected.

23:56.664 --> 23:58.437
I need Dr. Black Jack.

23:58.595 --> 23:59.955
Doc, come home.

24:00.469 --> 24:02.822
I might have an infectious disease.

24:03.101 --> 24:03.868
Doc!

24:04.142 --> 24:05.715
But you are my assistant!

24:05.842 --> 24:06.522
Let's see...

24:06.989 --> 24:07.809
Help...

24:08.195 --> 24:09.195
Did she die?

24:09.555 --> 24:11.597
It will become clear either today or tomorrow.

24:12.210 --> 24:14.477
Next Karte - The Cholera Epidemic.

24:16.170 --> 24:17.963
Karte NG...

24:19.090 --> 24:19.881
What?

24:19.882 --> 24:21.561
Do you have something to say?

24:22.006 --> 24:23.301
Shall we get ready for dinner?

24:23.332 --> 24:23.819
OK.

24:23.846 --> 24:24.725
Huh?
